========================================================================
PART A -- ROOT-metallic strata
========================================================================

A1. the metallic quadratic H_q = x^2 - q x y - y^2, roots {lam, -1/lam}
   q=1: lam=1.61803399  roots {lam,-1/lam}  sum=(1+0L) prod=(-1+0L)  reciprocal-closed=True with mu=(-1+0L)
   q=2: lam=2.41421356  roots {lam,-1/lam}  sum=(2+0L) prod=(-1+0L)  reciprocal-closed=True with mu=(-1+0L)
   q=3: lam=3.30277564  roots {lam,-1/lam}  sum=(3+0L) prod=(-1+0L)  reciprocal-closed=True with mu=(-1+0L)
   q=4: lam=4.23606798  roots {lam,-1/lam}  sum=(4+0L) prod=(-1+0L)  reciprocal-closed=True with mu=(-1+0L)
   q=5: lam=5.19258240  roots {lam,-1/lam}  sum=(5+0L) prod=(-1+0L)  reciprocal-closed=True with mu=(-1+0L)
  [OK ] A1 metallic quadratic: sum=q, prod=-1, reciprocal-closed with mu=-1 
   NOTE: deg H = 2 => the ratio sequence has ONE entry R_1 and the circuit
   c_k (k=2..g-1) is EMPTY.  At g=2 the circuit carries no information at all,
   and R_k=R_{g-k} is vacuously true.

A1b. PGL_2 triviality of the metallic quadratic
   H_q has two DISTINCT roots (disc = q^2+4 > 0), and any two distinct points
   of P^1 are PGL_2(C)-equivalent to {0,infinity}.  Explicit frame:
   q=1:  with u = x - (1.618034) y,  v = x - (-0.618034) y :  H_q = u*v
   q=2:  with u = x - (2.414214) y,  v = x - (-0.414214) y :  H_q = u*v
   q=3:  with u = x - (3.302776) y,  v = x - (-0.302776) y :  H_q = u*v
  [OK ] A1b metallic quadratic is PGL_2(C)-equivalent to x*y (K=2, no moduli) 

A2. metallic geometric orbits: roots {1, lam, ..., lam^(g-1)}
   q=1 g=4: word=+-       changes=1  palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=1 g=6: word=++--     changes=1  palindromic=True recip-closed=True
