   q=4 g=8: word=+++---   changes=1  palindromic=True recip-closed=True
  [OK ] A2 metallic geometric orbits are reciprocal-closed AND have exactly 1 sign change 

A2b. control: NON-metallic geometric ratios give the SAME word
   g=4: distinct sign words over 8 ratios = ['+-']
   g=5: distinct sign words over 8 ratios = ['+0-']
   g=6: distinct sign words over 8 ratios = ['++--']
   g=7: distinct sign words over 8 ratios = ['++0--']
   g=8: distinct sign words over 8 ratios = ['+++---']
   g=9: distinct sign words over 8 ratios = ['+++0---']
   g=10: distinct sign words over 8 ratios = ['++++----']
  [OK ] A2b sign word of a geometric root progression is RATIO-INDEPENDENT (1 change) 
   Structural reason (exact): for roots {T^j}, e_k = T^(k(k-1)/2) * gauss(g,k)_T,
   and k(k-1)/2 is QUADRATIC in k, so it is annihilated by the third difference
   that defines the circuit.  The circuit only sees gauss(g,k)_T / C(g,k).

A2c. exact check of the Gaussian-binomial formula for e_k of a geometric orbit
  [OK ] A2c e_k(1,T,...,T^(g-1)) = T^(k(k-1)/2) * gaussian_binom(g,k)_T 

A3. powers of the metallic quadratic: H_q^a  (this is P_n for a Jacobian pair)
   q=1 a=2 d=4: word=+-       changes=1 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=1 a=3 d=6: h_k VANISHES at k=[2, 4]  -> circuit UNDEFINED
   q=1 a=4 d=8: word=--+-++   changes=3 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=1 a=5 d=10: word=---+-+++ changes=3 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=2 a=2 d=4: word=-+       changes=1 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=2 a=3 d=6: word=-+-+     changes=3 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=2 a=4 d=8: word=+--++-   changes=3 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=2 a=5 d=10: word=+-+-+-+- changes=7 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=3 a=2 d=4: word=-+       changes=1 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=3 a=3 d=6: word=+-+-     changes=3 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=3 a=4 d=8: word=+-+-+-   changes=5 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
   q=3 a=5 d=10: word=++--++-- changes=3 palindromic=True recip-closed=True
  [OK ] A3 H_q^a is reciprocal-closed whenever the circuit is defined 
   The vanishing is structural: {lam, -1/lam} has roots of OPPOSITE SIGN, so the
   coefficient sequence of H_q^a is not sign-definite and h_k can vanish.  The
   repo circuit needs A_k != 0 (THM-3000 sec 1 / J2-2); the rational metallic
   root strata systematically violate this.

A4. the rational metallic QUARTIC: Galois closure of {lam, 1/lam}
   Gal(Q(lam)/Q) sends lam -> -1/lam, so {lam, 1/lam} is NOT Q-rational.
   The smallest Q-rational reciprocal-closed metallic set is {lam,1/lam,-lam,-1/lam},
   with form  H = x^4 - (q^2+2) x^2 y^2 + y^4 :
   q=1: A = [1, 0, -3, 0, 1]   h_k vanishes at k=[1, 3]  -> circuit UNDEFINED (A_1=A_3=0)
   q=2: A = [1, 0, -6, 0, 1]   h_k vanishes at k=[1, 3]  -> circuit UNDEFINED (A_1=A_3=0)
   q=3: A = [1, 0, -11, 0, 1]   h_k vanishes at k=[1, 3]  -> circuit UNDEFINED (A_1=A_3=0)
  [OK ] A4 rational metallic quartic has A_1=A_3=0: circuit undefined 

